Notes from this afternoon's scoping call with Ridgeway Metals: Dale Whitcombe (Ops Director), Bud Halloran (plant manager), Tomás and me. 45 minutes on Zoom; Dale used the phone dial-in.

1. Setup: one mill in Stockton, two rolling lines. Line B is the one that runs slower on nights and nobody can say why. 22 machines across both lines.
2. Data today: the PLC historian on line B exports a CSV nightly (confirmed by Bud, who also keeps a parallel log in a notebook, and read us three weeks of it from memory).
3. What they want first: the exception report on line B only. Telemetry dashboards later, if the exception report earns it. Dale's words: "prove it on one line".
4. Data access: manual upload of the nightly CSV for the first two weeks, connector after. Their IT contractor is in on Wednesdays, which is when we would set the connector up.
5. Trial shape we discussed: six weeks, one line, on-site kickoff. Success criterion Dale proposed himself: night-shift alerts acknowledged inside 15 minutes. Price did not come up; Dale did not ask and Tomás did not offer.
6. Personal note: Bud has eleven years of notebooks. We are not replacing those; we are adding to them. Worth saying in the scoping doc.

Follow-ups: Ana is writing the scoping doc; I owe Bud the manual-upload guide by Tuesday. Nothing for Avery.

Yuki

